k, Flint, Gamel, Habdel, Hardek, Lee'Delle, Memech, Morpel, Obi, Robert, Rock In A Hard Place, Romella, Rowenna, Sam, Shanar, Turvy, Ulrik, Uzgod, Willard","slot":"Weapon Hand","task_item":"yes","upgradeclass":"1","usable":"yes","value":"25 - 100","walkable":"yes","weapontype":"Club","weight":"39.00"},"page_id":2674,"revision_id":1202769,"revision_timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:44:20Z","wiki_title":"Bone Club"},"item_key":"oteryn:item.tibia.i3337","selected_historical":{"content_sha256":"9e0d68ee10cfb4c45f44cc49376df882137d1b8f95467419285145af25c721e9","page_id":2674,"revision_id":1202769,"revision_timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:44:20Z","title":"Bone Club"},"stackable":false},{"appearance_id":3365,"binding":{"disposition":"EXACT","external_id":"3365","identity_namespace":"ots/item_server_id","source_key":"oteryn:source.crystalserver","source_revision":"ff7ede593c69d4c658b382c97443e8155926924a","target":{"family":"Item","key":"oteryn:item.tibia.i3365","revision":"definition-r1"}},"current":{"content_sha256":"0e151bc9c1829856cdee68d4e7abea5bb84a2b32d71b48e2beedd694a2a0e0b7","page_id":2345,"revision_id":1207380,"revision_timestamp":"2026-09-29T12:52:13Z","title":"Golden Helmet"},"historical_observation":{"content_sha256":"0e151bc9c1829856cdee68d4e7abea5bb84a2b32d71b48e2beedd694a2a0e0b7","fields":{"actualname":"golden helmet","armor":"12","article":"a","buyfrom":"--","droppedby":"{{Dropped By|}}","flavortext":"It's the famous Helmet of the Stars.","getvalue":"{{{GetValue|}}}","history":"* This rare item was obtainable a long time ago from the [[Daemon]] until a later update. After the introduction of [[Character World Transfer]]s, more servers got access to this legendary helmet.\n* Its armor value was changed from 13 to 12 with [[Updates/7.0|Update 7.0]].\n* [[CM]] [[Skerio]] wrote on {{Post|39252841|November 21, 2021}}: ''\"(...) items which cannot be gained in the game any longer and have to be acquired from other players, e.g. golden helmet (...)\"'', which means that, as of that date, Golden Helmet was not lootable from bosses or quests.\n\n==== Story from Karl ====\n\nAn old story from Karl, former \"Wizard\" (that's what [[Gamemaster]]s were called a long time ago):\n<blockquote>\nBefore I begin, I have to point out that it was not really the first HOTS that was gotten by a player, but the first that still exists today. There was an update (in 1997 with client 2.0 ) where all now rare items were deleted and the whole setting of the item system was reformed. It was necessary, because it was very easy before to get those items (dragons dropped them all) and every level 5 player already had a full set of the (back then) best items in the game: HOTS, E-plate and a firesword. So to make Tibia more interesting, all these items where replaced by a steel helmet, a regular plate armor (or was it a chain armor?) and a regular sword. From that update onwards, the rare items were hard to come by. Maybe it was not as hard as it is today, but still a lot harder then before.<br/><br/>\nSo when the server came online with the new update, Thais was swarming with people filling the temple right away and giving good old Quentin a shock by the sudden appearance of so many players logging in at his residence. Some were upset by the now lame equipment they were wearing, some were rushing into the depot to check what happened in there. One player run ahead of all others to be the first at the demon to see what treasures he would hide. This was [[Galadriiell]], the probably mightiest sorcerer back then. She wouldn’t have had to hurry that much, because there was no one else that was so eager to see the big red one, but still she did. There was only one place in Tibia back then where you could encounter a demon, and that was deep below Thais, south of Mintwallin. It was not longer then 10-15 minutes after the server came online that I got a message from [[Galadriiell]]: she had defeated the demons and found as a treasure the famous Helmet of the Stars and an enchanted plate armor. She was a bit upset, because she thought it was still to easy to get the nice stuff. What we didn’t know then was that this mighty treasure only spawned once, so it was Galadriiell who was the first and only player that had these nice items for some time.\n</blockquote>\n\n==== Gallery ====\n<gallery mode=\"nolines\">\nFile:Daemon loot.jpg","imbueslots":"2","immobile":"no","implemented":"3.0","itemid":"3365","list":"{{{1|}}}","marketable":"yes","name":"Golden Helmet","notes":"Part of the [[Golden Set]]. It can be seen in [[Treasure Rooms#Hellgate Treasure Chamber|Hellgate Treasure Chamber]], [[Treasure Rooms#Morguthis Treasure Room|Morguthis Room]] and [[Treasure Rooms#Beregar Treasure Room|Pythius The Rotten's Treasure Room]].","npcprice":"0","npcvalue":"420","objectclass":"Body Equipment","pickupable":"yes","plural":"?","primarytype":"Helmets","sellto":"H.L.","slot":"Head","upgradeclass":"4","value":"1,000,000,000+","walkable":"yes","weight":"32.00"},"page_id":2345,"revision_id":1147406,"revision_timestamp":"2025-12-08T14:36:02Z","wiki_title":"Golden Helmet"},"item_key":"oteryn:item.tibia.i3365","selected_historical":{"content_sha256":"0e151bc9c1829856cdee68d4e7abea5bb84a2b32d71b48e2beedd694a2a0e0b7","page_id":2345,"revision_id":1147406,"revision_timestamp":"2025-12-08T14:36:02Z","title":"Golden Helmet"},"stackable":false},{"appearance_id":50239,"binding":{"disposition":"EXACT","external_id":"50239","identity_namespace":"ots/item_server_id","source_key":"oteryn:source.crystalserver","source_revision":"ff7ede593c69d4c658b382c97443e8155926924a","target":{"family":"Item","key":"oteryn:item.tibia.i50239","revision":"definition-r1"}},"current":{"content_sha256":"0031ea0f30982114f0aef2a50b85cd1f036e7b7937c264934f3ff487207a5ed2","page_id":108151,"revision_id":1207393,"revision_timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:21:47Z","title":"Amber Kusarigama"},"historical_observation":{"content_sha256":"82d4691ebcac5507f14a886be31a7a193d1d0829a13a250ad6642cad8eb3b75f","